    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current Pollution Under Control (PUC) Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A valid PUC certificate proves that the vehicle meets the environmental standards set by the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change. Transport companies typically require this certificate to avoid fines or delays at checkpoints.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The insurance policy should cover the vehicle for the entire duration of the transport, including loading, transit, and unloading. The certificate must state the policy number, coverage limits, and the insurer’s contact details. Ensure that the policy is active at the time of departure.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Bilty is a transport document that records the consignment details and is issued by the Indian Bureau of Shipping (IBA). An IBA‑approved Bilty is mandatory for road‑to‑marine or marine transits, and it serves as proof of the vehicle’s movement and ownership during the trip.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>In addition to these core documents, it is highly advisable to secure <strong>100% Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance</strong>. This type of insurance guarantees that the full market value of the vehicle is covered in the event of loss, theft, or damage while on the road or during any marine transit segment.</p>
<p>By declaring the vehicle’s full value, you eliminate the risk of under‑insurance and ensure that any claim will be settled at the vehicle’s true market price. Marine transit insurance also offers protection against unforeseen incidents such as accidents, natural calamities, or vandalism that may occur en route.</p>

<p>To summarize, the key paperwork for transporting a car from Delhi to Vijayawada includes a self‑attested RC photocopy, a current PUC certificate, a valid insurance certificate, and an IBA‑approved consignment bilty. Pairing these documents with 100% declared‑value marine transit insurance will safeguard your vehicle’s safety, legality, and financial integrity throughout the journey.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



